<Layout title="COMMET - Mas Muhammad" description="A Closed User Group (CUG) whitelist management system for Telkomsel telecom subscribers — processing SMS/USSD messages for subscriber registration, program offerings, and premium activations. Built with Oracle PL/SQL with SOAP-based API integrations.">
  <Nav variant="subpage" backHref="/portfolio" backText="Back to Portfolio" />

  <div class="cs-page">

<header class="cs-hero">
    <div class="cs-hero-meta">
      <span class="cs-badge cs-badge-corporate">Corporate</span><span class="cs-badge cs-badge-client">Telkomsel</span> 
      <span class="cs-badge cs-badge-year">July 2014</span>
      <span class="cs-badge cs-badge-critical">Mission Critical</span>
    </div>
    <h1 class="cs-hero-title">COMMET<span class="cs-cursor"></span></h1>
    <p class="cs-hero-desc">
      A Closed User Group (CUG) whitelist management system for Telkomsel telecom subscribers — processing SMS/USSD messages for subscriber registration, program offerings, and premium activations. Built with Oracle PL/SQL with SOAP-based API integrations.
    </p>
    <div class="cs-stack-pills">
      <span class="cs-stack-pill">Oracle PL/SQL</span>
      <span class="cs-stack-pill">SOAP/XML</span>
      <span class="cs-stack-pill">Oracle Database</span>
      <span class="cs-stack-pill">SMS Gateway</span>
    </div>
  </header>

  <img src="/gallery/commet.webp" alt="COMMET" class="cs-hero-img" loading="lazy" />

  <section class="cs-section">
    <div class="cs-section-label">
      <span class="cs-section-label-text">Impact</span>
      <div class="cs-section-label-line"></div>
      <span class="cs-section-label-num">01</span>
    </div>
    <div class="cs-metrics-grid">
      <div class="cs-metric-card">
        <div class="cs-metric-val">1,300+</div>
        <div class="cs-metric-label">Lines of Code</div>
        <div class="cs-metric-sub">Oracle PL/SQL</div>
      </div>
      <div class="cs-metric-card">
        <div class="cs-metric-val">5+</div>
        <div class="cs-metric-label">SOAP API Calls</div>
        <div class="cs-metric-sub">Outbound integrations</div>
      </div>
      <div class="cs-metric-card cs-red">
        <div class="cs-metric-val">8</div>
        <div class="cs-metric-label">Complexity Score</div>
        <div class="cs-metric-sub">Mission Critical</div>
      </div>
      <div class="cs-metric-card cs-amber">
        <div class="cs-metric-val">30+</div>
        <div class="cs-metric-label">Database Tables</div>
        <div class="cs-metric-sub">Oracle schema</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cs-section">
    <div class="cs-section-label">
      <span class="cs-section-label-text">Architecture</span>
      <div class="cs-section-label-line"></div>
      <span class="cs-section-label-num">02</span>
    </div>
    <div class="cs-arch-diagram">
      <div class="cs-arch-diagram-inner">

        <div class="cs-arch-node cs-source">
          <div class="cs-arch-node-icon"></div>
          <div class="cs-arch-node-label">SMS / USSD</div>
          <div class="cs-arch-node-sub">Subscriber input</div>
        </div>

        <div class="cs-arch-arrow">
          <div class="cs-arch-arrow-line"></div>
          <div class="cs-arch-arrow-label">keyword route</div>
        </div>

        <div style="display:flex; flex-direction:column; align-items:center; gap:0;">
          <div class="cs-arch-node core" style="width:220px;">
            <div class="cs-arch-node-label" style="font-size:13px; margin-bottom:10px;">PL/SQL Packages</div>
            <div class="cs-core-stack">
              <div class="cs-core-step">
                <div class="cs-core-step-dot"></div>
                Entry Layer · Keyword routing
              </div>
              <div class="cs-core-step">
                <div class="cs-core-step-dot"></div>
                Business Logic · CUG validation
              </div>
              <div class="cs-core-step">
                <div class="cs-core-step-dot" style="background:var(--blue)"></div>
                Utility Layer · SOAP dispatch
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="cs-arch-arrow">
          <div class="cs-arch-arrow-line"></div>
          <div class="cs-arch-arrow-label">SOAP/XML</div>
        </div>

        <div class="cs-arch-node cs-output">
          <div class="cs-arch-node-icon"></div>
          <div class="cs-arch-node-label">Telkomsel SOAP</div>
          <div class="cs-arch-node-sub">Region lookup · APIs</div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cs-section">
    <div class="cs-section-label">
      <span class="cs-section-label-text">Capabilities</span>
      <div class="cs-section-label-line"></div>
      <span class="cs-section-label-num">03</span>
    </div>
    <div class="cs-cap-grid">
      <div class="cs-cap-item">
        <div class="cs-cap-icon"></div>
        <div class="cs-cap-text">SMS keyword-based routing and procedure execution</div>
      </div>
      <div class="cs-cap-item">
        <div class="cs-cap-icon"></div>
        <div class="cs-cap-text">BTPN bank subscriber CUG whitelist registration</div>
      </div>
      <div class="cs-cap-item">
        <div class="cs-cap-icon"></div>
        <div class="cs-cap-text">Subscriber program offering lookup and eligibility</div>
      </div>
      <div class="cs-cap-item">
        <div class="cs-cap-icon"></div>
        <div class="cs-cap-text">Prepaid / postpaid premium offer activation</div>
      </div>
      <div class="cs-cap-item">
        <div class="cs-cap-icon"></div>
        <div class="cs-cap-text">Whitelist validation for closed user groups</div>
      </div>
      <div class="cs-cap-item">
        <div class="cs-cap-icon"></div>
        <div class="cs-cap-text">SOAP-based region lookup and API integrations</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cs-section">
    <div class="cs-section-label">
      <span class="cs-section-label-text">Decision Log</span>
      <div class="cs-section-label-line"></div>
      <span class="cs-section-label-num">04</span>
    </div>
    <div class="cs-decision-list">

      <div class="cs-decision-card">
        <div class="cs-decision-header">
          <div class="cs-decision-num">01</div>
          <div>
            <div class="cs-decision-title">Packaged Architecture — Standalone → Package-based Design</div>
            <div class="cs-decision-problem">
              v1.0 relied on standalone PL/SQL procedures with duplicated logic across modules — maintenance became increasingly fragile as the CUG rule set grew.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-decision-body">
          <div>
            <div class="cs-decision-col-label cs-chosen">▸ Chosen</div>
            <div class="cs-decision-col-text">
              Refactored into Oracle PL/SQL packages with a three-layer structure: entry routines for keyword routing, business logic for CUG validation, and utility procedures for SOAP dispatch. Centralized error handling and logging.
            </div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="cs-decision-col-label cs-tradeoff">▸ Trade-off</div>
            <div class="cs-decision-col-text">
              Required a full regression cycle across all SMS keyword flows. Package dependencies introduced stricter compilation ordering — mitigated by a build manifest that ensured correct deployment sequencing.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-decision-code">
<pre><span class="cs-token-cm">--  v1.0: standalone procedures, duplicated logic</span>
<span class="cs-token-kw">PROCEDURE</span> <span class="cs-token-fn">register_cug</span> (p_msisdn VARCHAR2) <span class="cs-token-kw">IS</span> ...
<span class="cs-token-kw">PROCEDURE</span> <span class="cs-token-fn">validate_cug</span> (p_msisdn VARCHAR2) <span class="cs-token-kw">IS</span> ...

<span class="cs-token-cm">--  v2.0: packaged, layered</span>
<span class="cs-token-kw">PACKAGE</span> <span class="cs-token-fn">commet_entry</span>  <span class="cs-token-kw">IS</span> ...  <span class="cs-token-cm">-- keyword routing</span>
<span class="cs-token-kw">PACKAGE</span> <span class="cs-token-fn">commet_biz</span>    <span class="cs-token-kw">IS</span> ...  <span class="cs-token-cm">-- business logic</span>
<span class="cs-token-kw">PACKAGE</span> <span class="cs-token-fn">commet_util</span>   <span class="cs-token-kw">IS</span> ...  <span class="cs-token-cm">-- SOAP dispatch</span></pre>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="cs-decision-card">
        <div class="cs-decision-header">
          <div class="cs-decision-num">02</div>
          <div>
            <div class="cs-decision-title">Integration Pattern — SOAP/XML over REST</div>
            <div class="cs-decision-problem">
              Telkomsel's existing infrastructure was built on SOAP-based middleware — REST endpoints were not available for CUG whitelist operations and region lookups.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-decision-body">
          <div>
            <div class="cs-decision-col-label cs-chosen">▸ Chosen</div>
            <div class="cs-decision-col-text">
              Native Oracle PL/SQL SOAP calls via <code>UTL_HTTP</code> + XML parsing with <code>XMLDOM</code>. Five outbound SOAP operations wrapped in dedicated utility functions with timeout and retry handling.
            </div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="cs-decision-col-label cs-tradeoff">▸ Trade-off</div>
            <div class="cs-decision-col-text">
              XML parsing in PL/SQL is verbose and resource-intensive compared to JSON. SOAP envelope construction required careful string handling. Mitigated by parameterized XML templates stored in database constants.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-decision-code">
<pre><span class="cs-token-cm">-- SOAP request via UTL_HTTP</span>
<span class="cs-token-fn">commet_util.soap_region_lookup</span>(
  p_msisdn =&gt; <span class="cs-token-str">'6281xxxx'</span>,
  p_result  =&gt; l_region
);

<span class="cs-token-cm">-- Parsed with XMLDOM</span>
l_node := <span class="cs-token-fn">XMLDOM.getNodeValue</span>(
  <span class="cs-token-fn">XMLDOM.getFirstChild</span>(l_elem)
);</pre>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="cs-decision-card">
        <div class="cs-decision-header">
          <div class="cs-decision-num">03</div>
          <div>
            <div class="cs-decision-title">SMS Keyword Routing — Prefix-based Dispatch</div>
            <div class="cs-decision-problem">
              Multiple CUG programs (BTPN bank registration, premium offers, whitelist validation) all shared a single shortcode — routing logic needed to parse SMS prefixes to determine the correct procedure.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-decision-body">
          <div>
            <div class="cs-decision-col-label cs-chosen">▸ Chosen</div>
            <div class="cs-decision-col-text">
              Keyword routing table driven: each SMS prefix mapped to a PL/SQL procedure via a lookup table. Adding new CUG programs required only a new table row and a targeted package procedure — no routing logic changes.
            </div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="cs-decision-col-label cs-tradeoff">▸ Trade-off</div>
            <div class="cs-decision-col-text">
              Keyword collisions required careful prefix design. Ambiguous prefixes would fall through to a default handler returning an error SMS. Mitigated by prefix length ordering: longer (more specific) prefixes matched first.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-decision-code">
<pre><span class="cs-token-cm">-- Routing table entry</span>
<span class="cs-token-kw">INSERT INTO</span> sms_keyword_routing
  (prefix, pkg_procedure, description)
<span class="cs-token-kw">VALUES</span>
  (<span class="cs-token-str">'DAFTAR'</span>,  <span class="cs-token-str">'commet_entry.register_cug'</span>,   <span class="cs-token-str">'CUG registration'</span>);
  (<span class="cs-token-str">'CEK'</span>,      <span class="cs-token-str">'commet_entry.check_offer'</span>,   <span class="cs-token-str">'Offer eligibility'</span>);
  (<span class="cs-token-str">'AKTIF'</span>,    <span class="cs-token-str">'commet_entry.activate_premium'</span>, <span class="cs-token-str">'Premium activation'</span>);</pre>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cs-section">
    <div class="cs-section-label">
      <span class="cs-section-label-text">Business Impact</span>
      <div class="cs-section-label-line"></div>
